Ticket #4471 contains **412 unique reports**. The export has 427 rows because 15 report IDs appear more than once. Each unique report is merged into #4471.

## Problems found

<ProblemSplit />

The shared parser reads month-first while the affected tenants write dates day-first. That cause spans app, email, and booking-v2 form reports. Booking-v3 forms create a separate problem: they tell people to enter month-first dates even though those tenants use day-first locales.

The intake tag is only a guess, not a cause. The five reports the desk noted as one-day moves remain within the parser group; they do not form a third cause in the tenant-and-channel analysis.

## Tickets

- [Shared parser reads month-first — 379 reports](https://github.com/akozubek-megadev/megadev3/issues/1)
- [Booking-v3 form hint conflicts with day-first locales — 33 reports](https://github.com/akozubek-megadev/megadev3/issues/2)

